<title>USA: Harris awards contract to DSP unit.</title>
<headline>Harris awards contract to DSP unit.</headline>
<dateline>CUPERTINO, Calif. 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harris Corp said it has awarded CTP Systems, a subsidiary of DSP Communications Inc, a multimillion dollar contract to provide wireless components for use in wireless telephone communication systems.</p>
<p>The components will be for the the unlicensed personal communications system (UPCS) 1.9 GHz frequency band, it said. The agreement, which is expected to be completed in 1997, is part of an ongoing joint development partnership between Harris and CTP.</p>
<p>The exact value of the contract was not immediately available.</p>
<p>(-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
